{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_18dac2031adf9d166e0abf0f43183bf212873bb2a10369f0841737f369dc045f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The evidence consists solely of README content; the repository appears to be a documentation-only resource list with no shipped software runtime evidenced in the provided slices."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35cec323b36298021d7c6d48a498a494a90d55a5d3c726e2b46a77f47152a36f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README displays a 'PRs Welcome' badge, states the repository is actively maintained and welcomes contributions, and invites mistake reports or suggestions via email at csjuyongjiang@gmail.com."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b55f3beb7dbd8c9227cc0a622dbfdfb4d18a69a9e4bb842d9623ac0580a05b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An 'Evaluation' resources section links to evaluation frameworks including bigcode-evaluation-harness, code-eval, lm-evaluation-harness, and OpenCompass."},{"claim_ids":["clm_814fa7ed045a48d6e4c0d5c4aedf78a321d37c803fbfdbef787965bb1a0dc075"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The resource list links to external leaderboards such as BigCodeBench, HumanEval, EvalPlus, CRUXEval, and the Open LLM Leaderboard for comparing code-generation model performance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1af251229d95c15684f7f6ae41e8730870a7d312a3b6da0bc0db976307525d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An 'Applications' section lists AI coding assistants such as GitHub Copilot and Tabby, with Tabby described as a self-hosted, open-source alternative to Copilot."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6c033f175abde19bc3131ceed997742765f9c0515dc72ae2faf9cf3c49d54b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes a four-stage training workflow for Code LLMs, where stages 1-2 are pre-training and stages 3-4 are post-training, with stages 2 and 4 optional; examples note StarCoder uses only stage 1 and Code Llama covers stages 2 and 3."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bd756fdafb6ab74578ba7f1f7ee8d51267cedeb4a5931c42e7228674cf2691e1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The acknowledgements state the resource collection was inspired by the Awesome-Code-LLM and LLMSurvey repositories."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c7b6cbd2d8d408bbb655bc120f25177019b4672c026dc877c6e931360eee9e8f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a curated collection of papers and resources on large language models for code generation, tied to a survey paper accepted by TOSEM."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca93c9b50b62e3e0c51b0eb6195e81753c3b34c86dc503c5f6d19359cac78755"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README organizes the paper list into sections including pre-training, instruction tuning, reinforcement learning with feedback, prompting, data synthesis, repository-level/long context, retrieval augmentation, autonomous coding agents, alignment, and evaluation/benchmarks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2bdae9e7c0fd0169710a1c9684343692969a00ed97e1cf7dd4d62be4115c2d7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The associated survey is 'A Survey on Large Language Models for Code Generation' by Jiang, Wang, Shen, Kim, and Kim, available as arXiv preprint 2406.00515 (2024)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_18dac2031adf9d166e0abf0f43183bf212873bb2a10369f0841737f369dc045f","clm_35cec323b36298021d7c6d48a498a494a90d55a5d3c726e2b46a77f47152a36f","clm_4b55f3beb7dbd8c9227cc0a622dbfdfb4d18a69a9e4bb842d9623ac0580a05b4","clm_814fa7ed045a48d6e4c0d5c4aedf78a321d37c803fbfdbef787965bb1a0dc075","clm_a1af251229d95c15684f7f6ae41e8730870a7d312a3b6da0bc0db976307525d6","clm_b6c033f175abde19bc3131ceed997742765f9c0515dc72ae2faf9cf3c49d54b6","clm_bd756fdafb6ab74578ba7f1f7ee8d51267cedeb4a5931c42e7228674cf2691e1","clm_c7b6cbd2d8d408bbb655bc120f25177019b4672c026dc877c6e931360eee9e8f","clm_ca93c9b50b62e3e0c51b0eb6195e81753c3b34c86dc503c5f6d19359cac78755","clm_d2bdae9e7c0fd0169710a1c9684343692969a00ed97e1cf7dd4d62be4115c2d7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_9cf79f171458461a8789daa6945ba66d","id":"pg_5e3e5c3bf4d75ef3931191cb53562173","maturity":"draft","page_type"